window.docContents[161].resolve({"/Taking-Terms-Apart/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-API-for-CVC5--Taking-Terms-Apart--Folding-and-Rewriting":{"contents":"Term.fold visits a term's nodes depth first, handing each to two optional functions with its\nview: pre on reaching the node, which may skip its kids or stop the fold, and post on leaving\nit. The typed layer has two more, prePlain and postPlain, for the nodes whose sort has no\nTyp — a quantifier's variable list, for instance.\n\nopen Typed in #eval Env.runIO do\n  let x ← Term.mkSymbolAs Int \"x\"\n  let y ← Term.mkSymbolAs Int \"y\"\n  let t ← smt! x < y ∧ y = x + 1\n  let syms ← t.fold #[] (pre := fun {τ} _ (v : V τ) acc =>\n    match τ, v with\n    | .int, .symbol x =>\n      if acc.contains x then return .descend acc\n      else return .descend (acc.push x)\n    | _, _ => return .descend acc)\n  println! \"integer symbols: {syms}\"\n\n\ninteger symbols: #[x, y]\n\n\nTerm.walk visits the nodes through a zipper, which also sees where the node sits, and may\nreplace a node. A typed node's replacement is a term of its sort, so a rewrite cannot build an\nill-sorted term; a sort-erased replacement is checked. post sees a node rebuilt with its replaced\nkids, so a bottom-up rewrite is a post alone — here, removing double negations:\n\nopen Typed in #eval Env.runIO do\n  let p ← Term.mkSymbolAs Bool \"p\"\n  let q ← Term.mkSymbolAs Bool \"q\"\n  let t ← smt! ¬ ¬ p ∧ ¬ ¬ ¬ q\n  let (s, _) ← t.walk () (post := fun {τ} _ (v : V τ) _ =>\n    match τ, v with\n    | .bool, .not t => do\n      match ← V.of .bool t with\n      | .not u => return .replace u ()\n      | _ => return .continue ()\n    | _, _ => return .continue ())\n  println! \"{t} ↦ {s}\"\n\n\n(and (not (not p)) (not (not (not q)))) ↦ (and p (not q))\n\n\nThe sort-erased layer works the same way, without the sorts: V.of is a pure function there, and\na fold runs in any monad.\n\n\n","context":"Cvc.lean -- High-Level API for CVC5\u0009Taking Terms Apart","header":"5.2. Folding and Rewriting","id":"/Taking-Terms-Apart/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-API-for-CVC5--Taking-Terms-Apart--Folding-and-Rewriting"}});